// 1998. Iris is thirty-seven: one day, six things that want her, and her father dying at St Anne's.

// The day mechanic offers the acts whose `at` holds the slot it is in, four slots, and the
// two-slot act takes two. Each act is offered once: its condition is that it is not yet kept.
// When the slots run out the mechanic goes on to `then`.
== day_1998
  [day] [slots morning, noon, afternoon, evening] [then day_end_1998]
Six things want her today. There is time for four.
  [prompt]
{ life = stay }
  + { kept hasnt ruth } Ruth's fever
    [at morning] [who Ruth]
    She sits on the end of Ruth's bed with a flannel and the radio. Ruth is asleep by eleven, holding her sleeve.
    [kept += ruth]
  + { kept hasnt stock } The stocktake at the shop
    [at morning, noon] [who the shop]
    Four hundred and twelve tins of peaches. Nobody buys peaches. She counts them anyway, because Dad would have.
    [kept += stock]
  + { kept hasnt dad } Visit Dad at St Anne's
    [at noon, afternoon] [who Dad] [marked]
    St Anne's is a bus and a walk. She runs the walk.
    [kept += dad]
    -> deathbed_1998 ->
  + { kept hasnt tom } Tom's football final
    [at afternoon] [who Tom]
    Tom scores in the second half and looks straight up at the stand. She is on her feet. She is the only one on her feet.
    [kept += tom]
  + { kept hasnt danny } Danny's birthday dinner
    [at evening] [who Danny]
    The cake sinks in the middle. Danny eats two slices of the crater and says it's the best part.
    [kept += danny]
  + { kept hasnt piano } An hour at the piano, alone
    [at noon, evening] [who herself]
    Thirteen years since she played. Her hands remember the first eight bars of something and nothing after. She plays the eight bars until it's dark.
    [kept += piano]
{ life = go }
  + { kept hasnt rehearsal } The last rehearsal
    [at morning] [who the music]
    The orchestra takes her second movement too fast. She stops them with one hand, and for a second the whole hall waits on her.
    [kept += rehearsal]
  + { kept hasnt leo } Leo's school play
    [at noon] [who Leo]
    Leo is a tree. He doesn't move for forty minutes. She has never seen anything so brave.
    [kept += leo]
  + { kept hasnt radio } The radio interview
    [at morning, afternoon] [who her name]
    They ask where her music comes from. She says a kitchen. They laugh. She doesn't.
    [kept += radio]
  + { kept hasnt dad } The train north to Dad
    [at noon, afternoon] [cost 2] [while on the train] [who Dad] [marked]
    Three hours north on the slow train. She reads the same page the whole way.
    [kept += dad]
    -> deathbed_1998 ->
  + { kept hasnt premiere } The premiere
    [at evening] [who the music]
    Her piece is played. The applause starts late, the way it does when people mean it. She takes the bow and walks straight out of the building.
    [kept += premiere]
  + { kept hasnt walk } An hour by the river, alone
    [at morning, afternoon, evening] [who herself]
    She walks by the river and thinks of nothing at all. It is the best hour of the year.
    [kept += walk]
// a slot with nothing it can hold
- (idle) There is nothing she can do with the {slot}. She sits in the kitchen and lets it pass.
  [idle]

// What she didn't do also happened.
== day_end_1998
  [card]
Everything she didn't do also happened.
  [pause 0.2]
{ life = stay }
  { kept hasnt ruth }  Ruth spends the morning at the neighbour's, watching the door.
    [who Ruth]
  { kept hasnt stock } The stocktake waits. The bank doesn't.
    [who the shop]
  { kept hasnt dad }   Frank Marlowe died at {dies_at} that night. The nurse said he asked for her twice.
    [who Dad] [marked]
  { kept hasnt tom }   Tom looks for her in the stand until half-time.
    [who Tom]
  { kept hasnt danny } Danny eats at the table alone and wraps her plate in foil.
    [who Danny]
  { kept hasnt piano } The piano stays shut. It has been shut for thirteen years.
    [who herself]
{ life = go }
  { kept hasnt rehearsal } They rehearse without her. The second movement stays too fast.
    [who the music]
  { kept hasnt leo }       Leo is a tree. He watches the empty chair the whole time and stays very still, so she'd be proud anyway.
    [who Leo]
  { kept hasnt radio }     The interview goes to someone else. So, slowly, does the next commission.
    [who her name]
  { kept hasnt dad }       Frank Marlowe died at {dies_at} that night, three hundred miles north. The nurse said he asked for her twice.
    [who Dad] [marked]
  { kept hasnt premiere }  The premiere goes ahead without her. The conductor takes her bow.
    [who the music]
  { kept hasnt walk }      There isn't an hour that's hers. There hasn't been for years.
    [who herself]
-> found_1998

// After his death each life finds the same fact its own way.
== found_1998
  [card]
{ life = stay }
  A week after the funeral she clears the till drawer at the shop. Under the float, an envelope, soft from being opened and folded and opened.
  Royal College of Music, 1958: “…pleased to offer Mr F. Marlowe a place, beginning in the autumn term…”
    [quoted]
{ life = go }
  A letter comes two days after the funeral, posted the day before he died. His handwriting has got very large.
  DAD: I had a place at the conservatory in '58. I gave it up when your mother was expecting Margaret. I'd do it again. Don't you dare.
{ carried has gave }
  She already knew. It doesn't help.
    [pause 0.3]
[carried += gave]
-> years

// The deathbed: what she knows from anywhere opens a line.
== deathbed_1998
  [talk] [picture deathbed_1998]
He is very thin. He knows her straight away.
DAD: { life = go: You came all this way. | You came. }
- (ask)
* Of course I came.
  DAD: Your mother used to say that. 'Of course.' As if nothing cost anything.
  -> ask
* How are you feeling?
  DAD: Like a man in a bed.
  -> ask
* { carried has play } Play something for me, Dad.
  [known play]
  [said += play]
  He lifts his hands off the blanket. His fingers move on nothing, slow and sure, the way they must have once.
  DAD: There. Did you hear it?
  -> ask
* { carried has gave } You gave it up for me.
  [known gave]
  [said += gave]
  DAD: I'd do it again.
    [pause 0.2]
  DAD: Don't you dare give yours up.
  { life = go }
    * I didn't.
        DAD: I know. I read about you. I cut it out.
        He shows her where, in the drawer, the clipping is.
  { life = stay }
    * I already did.
        He closes his eyes for so long she thinks he's asleep.
        DAD: Then you've got it to give back.
  -> ask
* Sleep, Dad. I'm here.
  He sleeps. She stays.
  Frank Marlowe died at {dies_at} that night, with the radio on and her hand on the blanket.
    [pause 0.4]
  <-
